## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/fetch.html
- Summary (EN): Fetch brings a chosen COP node's outputs into the current network so they can be used there. Changes made to the original target COP flow through to the Fetch node automatically.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Fetch importe les sorties d'un autre nœud COP dans le réseau courant et suit automatiquement ses modifications.

- Inputs meaning: ["none described on the page; the source is set through the COP Path parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["COP Path: COP node whose outputs are fetched; dragging a node into the field fills in its path", "Set Outputs from Selected COP: reads the target COP's signature and fills the Outputs count and output details", "Outputs: number of outputs to fetch from the target COP", "Source Port: 0-indexed number of the target COP output to fetch", "Output Label: name of the fetched output port; filled from the target COP but renamable", "Output Type: data type of the fetched output; filled from the target COP but changeable"]

- Caveats: ["If Source Port is off, outputs are matched by order; for example the third Fetch output pulls the target's third output", "Changing Output Type can cause an error if the source type cannot convert to the new type"]

